{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: When history shows a sharp drop (e.g., >5 EUR in 3 days) followed by low sentiment, the model underestimates the subsequent rebound magnitude and speed; apply a +3 to +5 EUR upward correction for days 10-20 of the forecast horizon.",
    "Adjust for 'flat-line' bias in volatile regimes: If the model forecast is nearly linear (slope < 0.05 EUR/day) while true outcomes exhibit high volatility (spikes > 5 EUR), replace the linear projection with a range-bound mean-reversion model centered on the 20-day moving average.",
    "Sentiment-weighted overshoot correction: When sentiment history is zero or near-zero but price history shows a recent spike, the model fails to anticipate the immediate pullback; reduce the first 5 days of the forecast by 2-4 EUR to account for the lack of immediate bullish sentiment.",
    "Horizon-specific trend reversal: For forecasts extending beyond 15 days, the model consistently underestimates the amplitude of cyclical recoveries; increase the forecast slope by 0.15 EUR/day for the second half of the 30-day window if the 18-day history ends below the 30-day average.",
    "Sentiment signal threshold: If the average sentiment over the last 5 days is below 0.10, the model's assumption of stability is invalid; apply a volatility buffer of ±4 EUR to the forecast range rather than a point estimate."
  ]
}
